Diagnostic Summary for Test C:
1. In the continuum (L = 11, N = 24), E_{12} = 0.665 stabilizes the denominator D(11) = 0.442,
   yielding R_spec = 9.27 (dimensionless O(1) ratio).
2. The ground-state gap damping factor Delta_2 = 1.37e-26 scales the entire tail envelope,
   producing E_2^{op}(24; 11) = 3.06e-26.
3. Consequently, tail extinction Pi_{j, tail}(L) -> 1 requires ONLY that R_spec(N; L) does not
   grow faster than 1/Delta_2 ~ 10^{26}, an astronomically generous stability condition.

